  <h2 id="revision">One-minute revision</h2>
  <Callout kind="revision">
    <ul>
      <li>Matrix: <Math tex="m \times n" /> table, rows × columns. <Math tex="A_{ij}" /> is row <Math tex="i" />, column <Math tex="j" />. Code counts from 0.</li>
      <li><Math tex="A\mathbf{x}" />: dot every row with <Math tex="\mathbf{x}" />. Also: a combination of the columns weighted by <Math tex="\mathbf{x}" />.</li>
      <li>Shape rule: <Math tex="(m \times n)(n \times p) = m \times p" />. Inner must match and vanishes. Write shapes first.</li>
      <li><Math tex="C_{ij}" /> = row <Math tex="i" /> of <Math tex="A" /> · column <Math tex="j" /> of <Math tex="B" />.</li>
      <li>Not commutative. Associative: bracket cheaply, <Math tex="B(A\mathbf{x})" /> for LoRA. Distributive. <Math tex="I" /> changes nothing.</li>
      <li>A matrix is a linear function; columns = where basis vectors land; multiplying = composing.</li>
      <li>Linear layer: <Math tex="XW^\top + \mathbf{b}" />, <Math tex="W" /> is (out, in), only the last axis changes. Parameters <Math tex="= \text{out} \times \text{in} + \text{out}" />.</li>
      <li><Math tex="(AB)^\top = B^\top A^\top" />. <Math tex="\mathbf{x}^\top\mathbf{y}" /> is the dot product. <Math tex="QK^\top" /> is <Math tex="n \times n" />, entry <Math tex="(i, j) = \mathbf{q}_i\cdot\mathbf{k}_j" />.</li>
      <li>Cost <Math tex="\approx 2mnp" /> FLOPs; forward pass ≈ 2 FLOPs per parameter per token; attention is quadratic in <Math tex="n" />.</li>
      <li><code>*</code> is element-wise, <code>@</code> is matmul. Broadcasting aligns from the right; size-1 axes stretch; use <code>keepdims=True</code>.</li>
    </ul>
  </Callout>
</Note>
